# L §4.4 "for that read", L §5.14.1 (tally 2.1.8 R13, #169-d; P11): `windows each` written on a low with no from
# splits as on the line: the read takes the day the line's run assigns. gift lands on wd, any day of
# 2026-03-28 .. 2026-04-03, with bonus_amt read there; the low over 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-02 is three runs under
# each axis option. 2.1.7's refcore replaced the line's assignment by the read's bare `each` and printed the plain
# form's holes.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-9): `low` and `next` are cut; the text is respelled as the `min` and the `first` they meant (L §5.14.1).
=== m.tally
model w_each
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis ax
  lo "low"
  hi "high"

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place work: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input wd: date
input rate: money PLN
input twice: int

def bonus_amt: money PLN at wd
  rule base = rate
  rule hi beats base = rate * twice when ax == hi

move gift: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from work to konto amount bonus_amt

ask lw: min(bal(konto, d) for d in 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-02 step 1 day) windows each

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wd = window(2026-03-28, 2026-04-03) "c"
  twice = 2 "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "own"

version r1
  cite card
  governs ..2026-03-31
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 10.00 PLN "c"

version r2
  cite card
  governs 2026-04-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 12.00 PLN "c"
=== expect
lw [wd = 2026-03-28 .. 2026-03-31] [ax = lo]: 10.00 PLN
  reading: ax = lo
  cut 2026-03-01
lw [wd = 2026-04-01] [ax = lo]: 12.00 PLN
  reading: ax = lo
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-01
  cut 2026-03-01
lw [wd = 2026-04-02 .. 2026-04-03] [ax = lo]: 0.00 PLN
  reading: ax = lo
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-02
  cut 2026-03-01
lw [wd = 2026-03-28 .. 2026-03-31] [ax = hi]: 20.00 PLN
  reading: ax = hi
  cut 2026-03-01
lw [wd = 2026-04-01] [ax = hi]: 24.00 PLN
  reading: ax = hi
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-01
  cut 2026-03-01
lw [wd = 2026-04-02 .. 2026-04-03] [ax = hi]: 0.00 PLN
  reading: ax = hi
  held: rate = 12.00 PLN (r2), read for 2026-04-02
  cut 2026-03-01
